UID:7f45db3f215f4df0@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 11/17/2026: Judicial Branch Ends Attorney Ent
 ry Screening Bypass Program and  Announces Procedure for Reimbursement
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nJudicial Branch Ends Attorney Entry Screening
  Bypass Program and  Announces Procedure for Reimbursement\nDate:\n11/17/2
 026\nBeginning January 1\, 2027\, attorneys entering state courthouses wil
 l no longer be able to bypass security screening. Attorneys who show their
  bar cards (which can be downloaded from the Board of Bar Overseers websit
 e) will be able to go to the head of the screening line.  In some courthou
 ses\, there may be a separate "attorneys only" line if resources allow.\nC
 hief Justice Stanfill spoke to the policy change: The Judicial Branch cont
 inuously reviews our security protocols to ensure appropriate measures are
  in place.  We believe this policy change provides greater protection for 
 all people using the courthouse. The policy change follows best practices 
 for courthouse security and aligns with the policy of the federal courts i
 n Maine and the state courts of most other New England states.\nThe Judici
 al Branch stopped issuing security cards to attorneys in May 2026. Attorne
 ys whose security cards have not expired by January 1\, 2027\, will be abl
 e to receive a pro rata refund of the fee for the unexpired portion. Instr
 uctions and the form for requesting a refund are posted on the For Attorne
 ys page of the Judicial Branch website and can be downloaded directly here
 :\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/attorneys/atty-security-card-reimbursement
 .pdf\nSupporting documents\nPress Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.
 gov/news/article.html?id=13368580
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13368580
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ab46174526511875@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 11/16/2026: Androscoggin County Courthouse to
  Undergo Remediation Efforts
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nAndroscoggin County Courthouse to Undergo Rem
 ediation Efforts\nDate:\n11/16/2026\nEnvironmental testing conducted after
  concerns were raised about the condition of the Androscoggin County Court
 house has revealed elevated levels of mold in some areas of the building. 
 The Judicial Branch ceased operations in all affected areas of the buildin
 g.  The Judicial Branch is working with Androscoggin County\, who owns the
  building\, to remove the mold and make needed repairs.  The building will
  be retested to make sure that the problems are eradicated before reopenin
 g any parts of the building with elevated mold levels.\nSupporting documen
 ts\nPress Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id
 =13368575
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13368575
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a37316cc847d4dc6@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 10/29/2026: Judicial Branch Announces Procedu
 re for Emergency Case Filings Regarding Elections
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome
 \n→\nNews & Announcements\nJudicial Branch Announces Procedure for Emerg
 ency Case Filings Regarding Elections\nDate:\n10/29/2026\nAUGUSTA\, Maine.
  The Maine Judicial Branch announced the procedure for emergency case fili
 ngs regarding elections to be held on November 3\, 2026.\nProcedure for El
 ection Filings\nIn order to expedite the review of filings\, Superior Cour
 t Chief Justice Robert Mullen and District Court Chief Judge Brent Davis i
 ssued a\nstanding order on October 28th\nrequiring\nall filings pertaining
  to the November 3 election and filed between Friday\, October 30\, 2026\,
  at 4:00 pm and Tuesday\, November 3\, 2026\, at 9:00 pm to be filed on pa
 per at the clerk's office.  Filers should NOT use the eFile Maine system\n
 for these emergency filings.\nFilings submitted on paper will be reviewed 
 immediately by a clerk and can be directed to the appropriate justice for 
 timely review.  Filers are also encouraged to put their cell phone numbers
  or emergency telephone numbers (where they can be reached after hours) on
  their filings.\nState Courts Open Late on November 3\nThe state courthous
 es in Bangor\, Augusta and Portland will be open until 9:00 p.m. for the p
 urpose of accepting and acting on emergency paper filings regarding electi
 ons.  A judge\, a clerk and a marshal will be on duty at each courthouse.\
 nAvailability of Documents to the Media\nAll public documents related to e
 lection filings will be posted on the high-profile page of the Judicial Br
 anchs public website as soon as is practicable.\nSupporting documents\nPre
 ss Release (PDF)\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=133656
 33
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13365633
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
